.SH EXIT STATUS
.nf
0 success
1 source-error-or-warning-denied
2 usage
3 environment-or-io
4 unsupported-target
5 toolchain
6 internal-compiler-error
.fi
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
JSON-lines schema 1 and SARIF 2.1.0 are selected explicitly. Source spans are UTF-8 byte ranges. LSP negotiates UTF-16 or UTF-8 positions.
.SH EDITS
format writes by default; select --check, --diff or --stdout to preview. Refactor rename previews unless --apply is explicit. Rejected edits preserve source bytes.
.SH OFFLINE FILES
share/diagnostics contains the compatibility registry and six general explanation records. Canonical native diagnostic codes and general explanation identifiers are distinct namespaces. No download is required.
